#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073450 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0be25cd8-4333-5e00-91e9-7e1256281814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "c4235bf2-0c2b-5c2d-be8d-779a8e5fb38f" :question/math-academy-id "e-13256" :question/problem "What ratio describes the number of pentagons to the total number of shapes?\n\n![](images/0f/0fff5dd90ce40b76128001c25b41cf8f34a2b4f63c44717823ba0bdcc98ef224.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the number of pentagons to the total number of shapes as follows:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{number of pentagons} : \\textrm{total number of shapes}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of pentagons. There are $3$ pentagons.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of shapes. There are $6$ shapes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of pentagons to total shapes is $3:6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073451 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acde6034-9007-5777-a79c-5f99ead9154a" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/id #uuid "76442c46-6958-556f-a895-027a3ce7427b" :question/math-academy-id "e-13257" :question/problem "A merchant has $8$ black crates and $5$ green crates. What ratio describes the number of green crates to the total number of crates?" :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the number of green crates to the total number of crates as follows:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{number of green crates} : \\textrm{total number of crates}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the number of green crates. There are $5$ green crates.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of crates. There are $8+5 = 13$ crates.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of green crates to total crates is $5:13.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073452 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073737 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9edb7c90-39fa-5396-b00e-04a0627d0581" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Ratios"}] :question/id #uuid "34ec50f1-1873-510d-8693-49f93bae1df8" :question/math-academy-id "e-13258" :question/problem "The ratio of red marbles to blue marbles in a  bag is $7:8.$ What is the meaning of this ratio?" :question/worked-solution "If the ratio of red marbles to blue marbles is ${\\color{red}{7}}:{\\color{blue}{8}},$ it means that there are ${\\color{red}{7}}$ red marbles for every ${\\color{blue}{8}}$ blue marbles."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434183 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073737 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9edb7c90-39fa-5396-b00e-04a0627d0581" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17eb0fde-642f-577d-8e69-073e8fb76929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434104} {:answer/id #uuid "1979cc03-76cd-553d-9f23-d5b593bf02cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434105} {:answer/id #uuid "93c9c22f-f585-5fdf-b2b4-d32640684b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434133} {:answer/id #uuid "e310d9e8-209d-561c-bea5-9568726c601a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434152} {:answer/id #uuid "e31b6f4d-7370-5a2d-9617-62891092ae97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e310d9e8-209d-561c-bea5-9568726c601a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434152} :answer-field/id #uuid "d752cf3e-67b8-5dd7-89f8-641e31fffc3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86a8860d-3cfb-576b-a5c9-f9833c8b5308" :question/math-academy-id "q-101428" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7b309bd6e44f1a1bc2e179dbcf50e6672366f69be364ae55b482cea16c680553.png)\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing numbers in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $4:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $\\,\\boxed{}\\,$ hexagons for every $1$ pentagon." :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the number of hexagons to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of hexagons}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of hexagons. There are $4$ hexagons.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There is $1$ pentagon.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $4:1.$\n\nSo, the missing numbers are  $1$ and $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0be25cd8-4333-5e00-91e9-7e1256281814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25dc957c-4c55-55c5-8e0b-4fa70c2cb1c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1:4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434108} {:answer/id #uuid "8973c614-3ce5-5be3-b379-8b3c32bbb81d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434130} {:answer/id #uuid "8bcf4156-e274-5ae9-b874-c7fe4d81b9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434131} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a