 is $2:7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434188 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acde6034-9007-5777-a79c-5f99ead9154a" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13757f22-4fab-5c53-b080-e053b71a28fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434102} {:answer/id #uuid "5f37b691-acd5-5c77-9ed1-9a12b7ec6c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434120} {:answer/id #uuid "82013105-0b25-5675-b6b1-ea0820db97b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434126} {:answer/id #uuid "9afb75fd-3f10-53e9-b9d5-a9768bcb7230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5:2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434135} {:answer/id #uuid "a9b4aff5-d3d9-5468-8b79-6c8de46a1837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13757f22-4fab-5c53-b080-e053b71a28fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434102} :answer-field/id #uuid "f68303ba-d3f6-5ad1-af0c-d38e73240e24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2300841-eb93-50ec-a81c-b69a7df78772" :question/math-academy-id "q-131946" :question/problem "To make a fruit sponge, Dimo mixes $3$ pounds of cherries with $2$ pounds of raisins. What ratio describes the amount of cherries to the amount of raisins?" :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the amount of cherry to the amount of raisins as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{amount of cherry}:\\text{amount of raisins}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the amount of cherries. There are $3$ pounds of cherries.\n\n- Next, we count the amount of raisins. There are $2$ pounds of raisins.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of cherries to raisins is $3:2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acde6034-9007-5777-a79c-5f99ead9154a" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1554d0b2-1daf-520d-b450-ef210692b911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434103} {:answer/id #uuid "5da73505-f24b-59ba-a3d9-9676f1617ce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434119} {:answer/id #uuid "86b7eb34-b85e-592c-9476-2afe1fb9c0a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434128} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd7da32-4128-5e21-9163-08566c170035" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1:2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434147} {:answer/id #uuid "e51adf65-6781-52c3-81a4-7511f4e2ed19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1:1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e51adf65-6781-52c3-81a4-7511f4e2ed19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1:1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434154} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f8fa62e-8a0c-5fc4-92ee-138c60b075b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "918c0ed9-8664-5aaa-af07-0b9b79fff05b" :question/math-academy-id "q-132025" :question/problem "To make waffles, Joshua mixes $5$ eggs, $1$ cup of sugar, $200$ grams of butter, and $1$ cup of flour. What ratio describes the amount of sugar to the amount of flour?" :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the amount of sugar to the amount of flour as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{amount of sugar}:\\text{amount of flour}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the amount of sugar. There is $1$ cup of sugar.\n\n- Next, we count the amount of flour. There is $1$ cup of flour.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of sugar to flour is $1:1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434182 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0be25cd8-4333-5e00-91e9-7e1256281814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e59982d-76f5-53c6-82c4-77f45fefe871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e59982d-76f5-53c6-82c4-77f45fefe871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434106} :answer-field/id #uuid "97c00a56-1f1a-5dcb-bee2-aa7a2a5e115b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7aee52c-482d-5af4-91e3-b6f75f9f1173" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7aee52c-482d-5af4-91e3-b6f75f9f1173" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434148} :answer-field/id #uuid "d68728f8-d9c4-5c99-9d25-510215e6c266" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "348bf862-0000-5608-8f25-158f815d9723" :question/math-academy-id "q-235814" :question/problem "![](images/38/38f113226c13332a07fdd6059819de5cf69147dbbfea3d1710325ef7776e5538.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the ratio of pentagons to the total number of shapes is{{field-1}}\n$:$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the number of pentagons to the total number of shapes as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of pentagons}:\\text{total number of shapes}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of pentagons. There are $4$ pentagons.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of shapes. There are $7$ shapes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of pentagons to the total number of shapes is $4:7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434189 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acde6034-9007-5777-a79c-5f99ead9154a" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd687c50-c716-5287-84f6-5b44539c34b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd687c50-c716-5287-84f6-5b44539c34b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434145} :answer-field/id #uuid "1895d3c9-f621-5af3-853c-714b8c6c27c9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434160} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83467b35-3621-505b-9ace-db58b87b47e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83467b35-3621-505b-9ace-db58b87b47e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434127} :answer-field/id #uuid "527131fb-44ca-5325-8aca-82b493559eb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e473c68b-cf42-5029-bb25-6a6af2c13e5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-235951" :question/problem "A study group contains $5$ freshmen, $4$ sophomores, and $3$ juniors. What ratio describes the number of freshmen to the total number of students?\n\nThe required ratio is{{field-1}}\n$:$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the number of freshmen to the total number of students as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of freshmen}:\\text{total number of students}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the number of freshmen. There are $5$ freshmen.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of students. There are $5+4+3=12$ students.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of freshmen to the total number of students is $5:12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073736 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acde6034-9007-5777-a79c-5f99ead9154a" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27ec799c-450f-552a-a2ad-1089fce23f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27ec799c-450f-552a-a2ad-1089fce23f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident 