ic is $2:5.$ What is the meaning of this ratio?" :question/worked-solution "If the ratio of dogs to total pets is $2:5,$ it means that there are $2$ dogs for every $5$ pets in the clinic.\n\nAnother way of writing this is to say that \"out of every $5$ pets in the clinic, $2$ of them are dogs.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0be25cd8-4333-5e00-91e9-7e1256281814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "484586d9-70ee-5024-80ae-ccaf354fb3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434114} {:answer/id #uuid "7c82b4c0-84bd-5405-80d1-8091a3ce8076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434123} {:answer/id #uuid "99282de8-8d77-589a-a7c6-b6b9108e6f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434134} {:answer/id #uuid "c38c972a-e116-5133-91a2-b9dcbb1d676e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434146} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd8a023-c330-50bb-b688-f4cfb0c2eca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99282de8-8d77-589a-a7c6-b6b9108e6f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434134} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bfb0685-209d-51d0-a308-fdff2aa4a1b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ff410a3-0c6f-5988-88a5-79160a3d1565" :question/math-academy-id "q-70129" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4f6801c9bb82b4ba0a3ac2d16bf9d06799d0349ff718fbc31429cd74d054bcbe.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of triangles to hexagons?" :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the number of triangles to the number of hexagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of triangles}:\\text{number of hexagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of triangles. There are $2$ triangles.\n\n- Next, we count the number of hexagons. There are $3$ hexagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of triangles to hexagons is $2:3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073735 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0be25cd8-4333-5e00-91e9-7e1256281814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "091970d9-19e9-5c8f-9d4c-37f6882cad35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434099} {:answer/id #uuid "3a497dcf-c546-5bfe-b3f0-5b5c87585083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434111} {:answer/id #uuid "4f589ac5-bc24-593f-b37d-f2e5a1dcae40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3:7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434115} {:answer/id #uuid "7fa16de3-c96a-532a-9d52-5b14d6061edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434125} {:answer/id #uuid "b22cc36c-f580-5ab5-9409-ef6f11721994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b22cc36c-f580-5ab5-9409-ef6f11721994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2:3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434139} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbc0948d-299a-5589-9b44-8aaa5970b041" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30f78782-46a8-5fef-93fa-62c3bc5d1001" :question/math-academy-id "q-70132" :question/problem "![](images/ea/eab3931ef4d46de23144f52420557e790a7e041231fec22d6819891e8e92ab16.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of hexagons to pentagons?" :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the number of hexagons to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of hexagons}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of hexagons. There are $2$ hexagons.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There are $3$ pentagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $2:3.$"}]}
